// until the exact encoded-response permit is acquired. Bounded control and
// interactive responses bypass that gate; these process-wide counters expose
// the remaining large-response queueing and codec cost so a future weighted
// reservation design can be judged with production data instead of inferred
// from end-to-end latency alone.
static RESPONSE_ENCODE_GATE_ACQUISITIONS_TOTAL: AtomicU64 = AtomicU64::new(0);
static RESPONSE_ENCODE_GATE_WAIT_US_TOTAL: AtomicU64 = AtomicU64::new(0);
static RESPONSE_ENCODE_DURATION_US_TOTAL: AtomicU64 = AtomicU64::new(0);
static PORT_FORWARD_BYTES_TOTAL: AtomicU64 = AtomicU64::new(0);
// Replaceable PTY state is intentionally best-effort. Keep explicit counters
// so operators can tell whether a path is fitting snapshots, using the
